================================================================================
 SCOPE
================================================================================

This AGPL-3.0 license applies ONLY to the Gotham mixnet crates:

    crypto-gotham             (protocol library)
    crypto-gotham-relay       (relay daemon)
    crypto-gotham-directory   (directory data model)
    crypto-gotham-authority   (directory authority server)

Each is dual-licensed. Its per-file SPDX header reads:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later OR LicenseRef-Gotham-Commercial

You may use these crates under EITHER the AGPL-3.0-or-later (this file) OR the
commercial license (see LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md), at your choice.

The Crypto application (crypto-proto, crypto-agent, crypto-store, crypto-tests,
crypto-enterprise, crypto-licensor, crypto-admin, crypto-tauri) is NOT under
the AGPL — it is proprietary. See LICENSE and LICENSE-PROPRIETARY.md.

================================================================================
 KEY CONSEQUENCE OF THE AGPL (network-use / "SaaS" clause)
================================================================================

The AGPLv3 differs from the GPLv3 in one decisive way: running a MODIFIED
version of the program to provide a service over a network counts as
"conveying" it. Concretely, if you operate a modified Gotham relay, directory,
or authority as a network service, you MUST offer the users of that service the
complete corresponding source code of your modified version, under the AGPLv3.

Running the UNMODIFIED official binaries imposes no source-disclosure
obligation on you — you are simply running the program.

